<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:56:56Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Japan's empty temples seek new ways to survive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a9bc263b4e2a3ff905b0d794fd62a45b9fc724a8ef41386f83200851a0b1b7f</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:56:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-s-empty-temples-seek-new-ways-to-survive/a-79157964--7eea677a26bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-s-empty-temples-seek-new-ways-to-survive/a-79157964?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With a declining population, shrinking congregations and growing economic pressures, temples are struggling to stay relevant. As more temples are sold or closed, is religion in decline in modern Japan?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US-Canada tariff dispute weighs on cross-border ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c4ce66833f2a230d6112775a8fe034eedb9242b3c663b33860b84593a013c69</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:56:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T10:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-canada-tariff-dispute-weighs-on-cross-border-ties/a-78815803--082b25646c1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-canada-tariff-dispute-weighs-on-cross-border-ties/a-78815803?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Canada's retaliatory tariffs take effect, Canadian and US car industries fear the trade war will hit them hard, while Canadians are cutting back on travel.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya: Crackdown on foreign traders prompts xenophobia fears</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34aefad9a9b99f082d5b6d7bc4dda2590738726a9c65fb970776774054a1dc04</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:56:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kenya-crackdown-on-foreign-traders-prompts-xenophobia-fears/a-79143847--a8e571d0a365.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-crackdown-on-foreign-traders-prompts-xenophobia-fears/a-79143847?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fears of xenophobia are rising in Kenya after President William Ruto ordered a crackdown on foreigners working as hawkers. The government insists however that legally documented foreign traders remain protected.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>3 years on, Morocco earthquake victims still wait for help</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cd5d0eb1d16dd6a61a0422bba2fbed8ac033d522d88f0d9092dcb5bdca62054</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T18:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/3-years-on-morocco-earthquake-victims-still-wait-for-help/a-78874844--12aebab2298e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/3-years-on-morocco-earthquake-victims-still-wait-for-help/a-78874844?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Reconstruction has progressed in the three years since the 2023 Morocco earthquake, but some survivors are still living in tents. Locals are divided as to how successful it's been, and whether state aid is enough.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Nicaragua challenges German arms exports to Israel at ICJ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ecf80da667eb3a8be4aad1ab557ee5513c47476f1b3df4d6a27501688f5cc3e</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-challenges-german-arms-exports-to-israel-at-icj/a-79148044--315737afbbdd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-challenges-german-arms-exports-to-israel-at-icj/a-79148044?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has asked the International Court of Justice to dismiss the case on jurisdiction grounds. It also said its arms exports to Israel were documented, published, and subject to more stringent checks than most.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>War criminal Ratko Mladic buried with military honors in Belgrade, Serbia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2cf4636c25c253204212c390cc4c842523c9872f27a70998fbac55a25ab2dcf5</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T15:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/war-criminal-ratko-mladic-buried-with-military-honors-in-belgrade-serbia/a-79148678--c4979d87a1d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/war-criminal-ratko-mladic-buried-with-military-honors-in-belgrade-serbia/a-79148678?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ratko Mladic, the former Bosnian Serb commander convicted of genocide in Srebrenica, has been buried in Belgrade. The funeral, broadcast live on TV, comes just days before President Vucic is expected to call an election.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan: Can creating new provinces fix governance?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3659f2782c5ad29c473a364f0f99b83eaa3c8a1d2f4f6ea0509007fc3cd41844</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T13:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-can-creating-new-provinces-fix-governance/a-79148059--3974ef70363a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-can-creating-new-provinces-fix-governance/a-79148059?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pakistanis broadly agree that the country needs more responsive and effective government, but many question whether simply creating more provinces is the solution.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Threatening letters revive fears among Kashmiri Pandits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c1211b1dcb5a6f0a092ebe6d311ee00574bb0a82d42fe1080fa98e699b7d39c</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T12:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/threatening-letters-revive-fears-among-kashmiri-pandits/a-79144481--ac4e07371076.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/threatening-letters-revive-fears-among-kashmiri-pandits/a-79144481?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Leaked addresses and phone numbers have reignited fears among Hindu government employees who returned to Muslim-majority Kashmir under a rehabilitation scheme.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys Witkoff and Kushner hold Ukraine talks after meeting Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64b9cb1112024ae2953cdd27f6bf5c3cf7e46861ad850edba3b9f867d6d7eee2</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T22:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779--687b66a14041.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner held talks with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy in Kyiv, seeking to revive efforts to end the war. But the latest diplomatic push seems to have produced no breakthrough.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany, Kosovo unite against ticks carrying deadly virus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c913d7cd0e83a8dc9fe505243e582fef7c73b3212f4031f9072eea2c885115dd</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223--2c267f5d11c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-kosovo-unite-against-ticks-carrying-deadly-virus/a-78655223?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has high-security labs while Kosovo has Hyalomma ticks and experience with the deadly Crimean-Congo hemorrhagic fever. Working together, German and Kosovar scientists are fighting the disease and its vectors.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>How climate change and food insecurity could fuel future conflicts</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c5fbf0b2d2683c397926d651dbcdc473bd4a6395304312ad305c7faa3fc1321</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T07:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-and-food-insecurity-could-fuel-future-conflicts/a-78871431--8e63f64c4115.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-climate-change-and-food-insecurity-could-fuel-future-conflicts/a-78871431?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Climate change, conflict, and trade tensions are putting pressure on the global food system. New research suggests the biggest risk is not food shortages, but whether societies can peacefully adapt to change.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
